---
source: crates/vps-ready/src/modules/ssh_bruteforce/tests.rs
expression: plan
---
modules:
  - id: ssh.bruteforce
    title: Ban addresses that keep failing to log in over SSH
    status: applicable
    changes:
      - id: "package:nftables,python3-systemd,fail2ban"
        summary: "install nftables, python3-systemd, fail2ban"
        diff: ~
        reversibility: partial
      - id: "file:/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/90-vps-ready.local"
        summary: "create /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/90-vps-ready.local (0644 0:0)"
        diff: "@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+# Written by vps-ready (ssh.bruteforce). `vps-ready rollback --last`\n+# restores the previous state; edits here are replaced by the next apply.\n+[DEFAULT]\n+banaction = nftables\n+backend = systemd\n+\n+[sshd]\n+enabled = true\n+ignoreip = 127.0.0.1/8 ::1 192.0.2.10\n"
        reversibility: reversible
      - id: "service:fail2ban.service"
        summary: enable and start fail2ban.service
        diff: ~
        reversibility: reversible
    reloads:
      - fail2ban-restart
    notes:
      - "the jail never bans 192.0.2.10, the address of this SSH session"
      - "if this installs fail2ban, rollback leaves it installed and enabled, as the package sets it up, so it runs the distro's own jails after a reboot; `systemctl disable --now fail2ban` turns it off"
